  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Added\n- SignatureMedian.ComputeMediansByRadius(R) overload (R → W conversion with validation).\n- IngredientRatioValidator to centralize validation and canonical error messages (CSV/Excel/UI), plus MessageOnceGate and KernelWidthFromRadius.\n\nChanged\n- All call sites now pass window width W (2 × R + 1) to SignatureMedian.ComputeMedians; UI shows Kernel Width.\n- CsvBrewService/ExcelBrewService validate smoothing parameters via IngredientRatioValidator for consistent behavior and messages.\n- CSV/Excel headers include both Kernel Radius (R) and Kernel Width (W).\n- Documentation (README, API Reference, XML) updated to reflect kernelWidth semantics and new validator/overload.\n\nFixed\n- Under-smoothing where radius R was erroneously passed to the width-based API.\n- Duplicate parameter-error dialogs by surfacing a single InvalidOperationException and showing its message once in the UI.",
